+The source support boundaries are platform- and API-specific; this table is not
+native execution or recovery qualification evidence:
+
+| API | Unix source behavior | Windows source behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `CognitiveStore::open` | Ordinary path-based open, bootstrap/migration and integrity checks; no independent current-cut admission | Ordinary path-based open and integrity checks; no descriptor-bound recovery guarantee |
+| `CognitiveStore::open_read_only_recovery` | Bounded retained-descriptor cold image, no sidecars, exact current-cut admission; no writer conversion | Descriptor binding returns `Indeterminate`; no recovered image |
+| `CognitiveStore::open_with_recovery` | Retained-descriptor private-copy recovery with the authority, fencing and activation checks above | Descriptor binding returns `Indeterminate`; no recovered writer |
+| `SqliteConfig::open_immutable_recovery_pool` / `open_identity_bound_durable_evidence_pool` | After identity revalidation, return `Unavailable`; general descriptor-backed VFS pools remain unimplemented | No valid recovery guard can be established; descriptor binding/revalidation returns `Indeterminate` |
+
+The Windows branches of the lower-level cold-image and recovery-copy helpers
+also return `Unavailable`. The existing Windows path/reparse-point checks and
+directory barriers do not supply the missing retained-handle backend. Windows
+recovery remains unimplemented: it requires qualified parent/database/sidecar
+identity retention, private ownership/ACL and link validation, bounded copying,
+and safe activation/durability semantics before any positive admission claim.
+These are implementation prerequisites, not completed work or permission to
+weaken `Indeterminate` checks.
+
+Ordinary reopening of an unchanged seeded store and observing the same anchor
+is a persistence control, not recovery admission or a fallback for a rejected
+image. Separately, `hepta-operations::DurableOperationStore::open` opens its own
+path-based SQLite store and performs expired-lease recovery. That lease/effect
+reconciliation is not Memory's descriptor-bound current-cut recovery. Unknown
+effects remain `Indeterminate` and require independent terminal reconciliation;
+a Memory recovery implementation does not by itself qualify Operations backup
+restoration or authorize redispatch.
